  "description": "Translate QuerySpec filter specifications into LINQ expression trees that Entity Framework Core turns into SQL. 50+ operators (comparison, string, collection, temporal, null/membership, regex, geospatial), nested AND/OR/XOR groups, and a compiled-expression cache that keeps translation cheap on hot paths. Use this when filter or sort input comes from an HTTP request, a saved view, a rules engine, or a config file — instead of writing expression trees by hand or interpolating SQL strings. Tested against the EF Core In-Memory, SQLite, SQL Server, and PostgreSQL providers. Multi-targets .NET 8 (LTS), .NET 9, and .NET 10 (LTS).",
